fixed his rudder

565
00:31:07,333 --> 00:31:09,033
我们已经晚了。
we were running late.

566
00:31:09,067 --> 00:31:11,233
而且潮水正涨。
And the tide was coming in.

567
00:31:11,267 --> 00:31:13,300
-八点差十。
-嗯。
-It's ten to eight.
-Yeah.

568
00:31:13,333 --> 00:31:14,833
还有22英里。
It's 22 miles.

569
00:31:15,767 --> 00:31:19,433
要是我的能行，那就是25分钟。
If mine works,
that's 25 minutes.

570
00:31:19,467 --> 00:31:20,667
梅：你觉得它有多快？
MAY: How fast
do you think it goes?

571
00:31:20,667 --> 00:31:22,033
-40节。
-梅：别闹！
-40 knots.
-MAY: Get off!

572
00:31:22,067 --> 00:31:23,667
(BOTH LAUGHING)
(BOTH LAUGHING)

573
00:31:23,667 --> 00:31:25,700
你看到它后面那台巨大的发动机了吗？
Have you seen
the size of the engine
on the back of it?

574
00:31:25,733 --> 00:31:27,567
-你的最高时速？
-慢得要命。
-Your top speed?
-Very slow.

575
00:31:27,667 --> 00:31:29,267
-四节。
-是的。
-Four knots.
-Yeah.

576
00:31:29,300 --> 00:31:32,033
而且潮水只有三节，约每小时一英里。
And there's
a three-knot tide.
It's a mile an hour.

577
00:31:32,067 --> 00:31:33,133
是啊。
Yeah.

578
00:31:33,167 --> 00:31:34,833
-那你呢？
-20节。
-And you?
-20 knots.

579
00:31:34,867 --> 00:31:36,867
别啊，詹姆斯。
No, James.

580
00:31:36,900 --> 00:31:39,667
听着，重点是，我是唯一还有点模糊希望的
Look, the point is
I'm the only one with
even a vague hope

581
00:31:39,667 --> 00:31:41,667
能在天黑前到达的。
of getting there
before nightfall.

582
00:31:41,667 --> 00:31:43,367
我们干脆等潮退再走吧？
Why don't we just
go when the tide's
going out?

583
00:31:43,400 --> 00:31:44,567
那时候会帮我们的。
Then it'll help us.

584
00:31:44,667 --> 00:31:46,533
-好主意。
-明天吧。
-That's a good idea.
-That's tomorrow.

585
00:31:46,567 --> 00:31:48,033
不，是静潮。
No, slack water.

586
00:31:48,067 --> 00:31:49,667
或者说，静潮，没错。
Or slack water, yeah.

587
00:31:49,667 --> 00:31:52,800
静潮大约明天一点左右。
那时候我们就去！
Slack water is tomorrow
about 1:00.
We shall go then!

588
00:31:52,833 --> 00:31:54,567
-好！
-我们现在去酒吧吧。
-Yes!
-We'll go to the pub now.

589
00:31:54,667 --> 00:31:56,433
-听起来不错。对。
-我们现在去酒吧。
-Sound idea. Yeah.
-We'll go to the pub now.

590
00:31:56,467 --> 00:31:59,033
然后明天一点。
And then tomorrow, 1:00.

591
00:31:59,067 --> 00:32:00,400
那就是我们在静潮的时候。
That will be us
at slack water.

592
00:32:00,433 --> 00:32:01,767
因为水面平静。
Because the water is slack.

593
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:04,533
什么是静潮？
What's slack water?

594
00:32:04,567 --> 00:32:06,133
(CLARKSON LAUGHING)
(CLARKSON LAUGHING)

595
00:32:06,167 --> 00:32:07,700
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

596
00:32:13,100 --> 00:32:15,800
说实话，横渡英吉利海峡简直是史上最蠢的想法。
Honestly, crossing The Channel

597
00:32:15,833 --> 00:32:18,900
就是那种感觉，整天都在想，
has got to be just about
the stupidest idea ever.

598
00:32:18,933 --> 00:32:21,033
"我今天会因为低体温，挂上胃泵。"
It's just one of those days
where you've just had
that sense,

599
00:32:21,067 --> 00:32:24,933
简直糟透了。
"I'm going to end up today
with hypothermia attached
to a stomach pump."

600
00:32:24,967 --> 00:32:25,967
Just awful.
Just awful.

601
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:27,900
我们都紧张得要命，怕车沉下去，
We were all so paranoid
about sinking,

602
00:32:27,933 --> 00:32:31,000
所以我们把那堆泡沫塞到每个角落，让它们漂得更好。
that's why we put
all that foam everywhere,
to make them float better.

603
00:32:31,033 --> 00:32:33,667
我们把泡沫缠在歧管上，缠在排气管上，
We wrapped it
around the manifold,
around the exhaust,

604
00:32:33,700 --> 00:32:36,200
缠在发动机上，任何超热的地方都不放过，
around the engine,
around anywhere
really hot,

605
00:32:36,233 --> 00:32:39,667
基本上，这就是为什么会冒出一大堆烟的原因。
basically, which is why
there was all that smoke
pouring out.

606
00:32:39,667 --> 00:32:43,733
好了，是时候给我们这辆性价比超高的车装上星标了。
Anyway, it's now time
to put a star in our
reasonably priced car.

607
00:32:43,767 --> 00:32:47,033
今晚我的嘉宾，曾被 Channel 4（第四频道）停职，
My guest tonight
was once suspended
from Channel 4

608
00:32:47,067 --> 00:32:52,267
因为在戒严线前的直播里说了 F——（脏话）。
for using the F-word
on live television
before the watershed.

609
00:32:52,300 --> 00:32:54,400
-我的天，真是...太...！（观众笑）
-I mean, for...sake!
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

610
00:32:54,433 --> 00:32:56,567
女士们先生们，Jools Holland（朱尔斯·霍兰德）登场。
Ladies and gentlemen,
Jools Holland.

611
00:32:56,667 --> 00:32:58,067
（观众欢呼）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

612
00:33:01,133 --> 00:33:03,767
-哟，这可是大玩意儿！-哦，见到你真高兴。
-Oh, this is something!
-Oh, lovely to see you.

613
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:05,867
是啊，感觉像是理查德·哈蒙德，
Yes, it's like
Richard Hammond,

614
00:33:06,667 --> 00:33:08,833
小得可怜，娇滴滴的。
so small and dinky.

615
00:33:08,867 --> 00:33:09,833
请坐。
Have a seat.

616
00:33:09,867 --> 00:33:12,433
非常感谢，我会的。
Thank you very much.
I shall.

617
00:33:15,667 --> 00:33:17,433
现在，你的体型跟理查德·哈蒙德一样。
Now, you're the size
of Richard Hammond.

618
00:33:17,467 --> 00:33:19,933
-是的。-不过回头看看你的前世，
-Yes.
-But looking
into your past life,

619
00:33:19,967 --> 00:33:22,800
老英式摩托车，弹钢琴，
old British motor bikes,
you play the piano,

620
00:33:22,833 --> 00:33:24,667
对外国食物总是抱持疑虑，
you view foreign food
with a suspicion,

621
00:33:24,700 --> 00:33:26,733
你说人们不该在假期出国旅行
you say that people shouldn't
go abroad on their holiday

622
00:33:26,767 --> 00:33:28,800
应该把假期花在车库里。
but should spend it
in the shed.

623
00:33:28,833 --> 00:33:31,100
我想我们跟詹姆斯·梅是出生时就被分开的。
Separated at birth,
I think, from James May.

624
00:33:31,133 --> 00:33:32,833
真是个可爱的小家伙。
What a lovely fellow he is.

625
00:33:32,867 --> 00:33:36,667
那人真是才华横溢，脑子灵光。
What a talented
and great mind that man has.

626
00:33:36,667 --> 00:33:39,000
不过，我真的很难把这些观念调和在一起，
It's very hard, though, for me
to reconcile these views

627
00:33:39,033 --> 00:33:41,067
因为我第一次看到你的印象是，
with how I first
remember seeing you

628
00:33:41,100 --> 00:33:44,200
在《The Tube》上，那简直是一场彻底的混乱。
on The Tube, which was,
of course, complete anarchy.

629
00:33:44,233 --> 00:33:46,033
好吧，那是早期的美好日子。
Well, that was
in early happy days.

630
00:33:46,067 --> 00:33:49,567
我觉得，从很多角度来看，那是电视第一次被
I think, in many ways,
that was the first time
that television was put

631
00:33:49,667 --> 00:33:51,900
交到疯子们手里。
into the hands
of the lunatics.

632
00:33:52,667 --> 00:33:54,567
现在情况已经不同了。
Now things have changed.

633
00:33:55,167 --> 00:33:56,467
（笑声）
(LAUGHING)

634
00:33:56,500 --> 00:33:59,100
好吧，那是它第一次大概发生的时候。
Well, it was the first time
it sort of happened.

635
00:33:59,133 --> 00:34:01,567
我们边走边编，而且全程直播。
And we made it up
as we went along
and it was live.

636
00:34:01,667 --> 00:34:03,267
而且那天是周五，
And it was Friday,

637
00:34:03,300 --> 00:34:04,900
当时是五点半，酒吧已经开门。
it was 5:30,
the pubs were open.

638
00:34:04,933 --> 00:34:07,467
你得在一分钟内完成所有采访。
You had to do
all of the interviews
in a minute.

639
00:34:07,500 --> 00:34:08,700
好吧，这还有另一件事，
Well, that was
the other thing,

640
00:34:08,733 --> 00:34:11,533
因为那算是青少年电视节目，我想，
because it was
youth television, I suppose,

641
00:34:11,567 --> 00:34:12,967
青春电视的开场，
the beginning
of youth television,

642
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:14,933
他们以为大家的注意力能撑这么久。
they thought everybody's
attention span was that long.

643
00:34:14,967 --> 00:34:17,200
所以我们只有一分钟的时间来做任何事。
So, we only had
a minute to do anything.

644
00:34:17,233 --> 00:34:18,833
我们请来了迈尔斯·戴维斯，
We had Miles Davis,

645
00:34:18,867 --> 00:34:21,467
这位史上最伟大的爵士传奇之一，
one of the great jazz legends
of all time, come up,

646
00:34:21,500 --> 00:34:24,100
而且他还在宣传自己的画作。
and he'd been promoting
his drawings.

647
00:34:24,133 --> 00:34:25,667
于是他坐了下来。
So he sat down.

648
00:34:25,700 --> 00:34:27,133
他们说：“你只有一分钟的时间采访他。”
They said, "You've got a
minute to interview him."

649
00:34:27,167 --> 00:34:29,667
我说：“可是他可是爵士乐史上最大的名字之一啊。”
I said, "But he's one of the
biggest names in jazz ever."

650
00:34:29,667 --> 00:34:34,433
我又说：“他肯定值不了一分钟吧。”
I said, "Surely he's worth
more than a minute."

651
00:34:34,467 --> 00:34:36,533
他们说：“好吧，给你一分钟二十秒。”
They said, "All right,
you can have a minute and 20."

652
00:34:38,233 --> 00:34:39,967
于是我坐下来，对他说，
So I sat and I said to him,

653
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:43,667
“嗯，戴维斯先生……” 他说那副酷炫的墨镜。
"Well, Mr Davis..."
He's just got these great
sort of sunglasses.

654
00:34:43,700 --> 00:34:47,467
我问：“你会把你的艺术和音乐联系起来吗？”
I said, "Would you connect
your art to your music?"

655
00:34:48,033 --> 00:34:50,167
他答道：“嗯……”
He said, "Hmm..."

656
00:34:51,933 --> 00:34:55,467
(模仿迈尔斯·戴维斯) “我会把我的艺术和音乐联系起来吗？”
(IMITATES MILES DAVIS)
"Would I connect my art
to my music?"

657
00:34:56,500 --> 00:34:58,167
CLARKSON: 别在意疼痛。
CLARKSON: Ignore the pain.

658
00:34:59,867 --> 00:35:03,667
“是啊，这可是个好问题。”
"Yeah.
That's a good question."

659
00:35:05,133 --> 00:35:07,167
我心里想……我可不想打断他。
And I'm thinking...
I don't want to interrupt.

660
00:35:07,200 --> 00:35:10,667
他接着说：“我会把我的艺术和音乐联系起来吗？
And he said,
"Would I connect
my art to my music?

661
00:35:12,667 --> 00:35:15,200
“好。”随后那位女士…
"Good."
And then the
woman behind...

662
00:35:15,233 --> 00:35:17,133
他们大概已经在这里准备好了。
They probably have them here.

663
00:35:17,167 --> 00:35:19,033
其实他们现在可能已经在做了，我正说得口水都快说完了。
They're probably doing it now,
actually, as I'm saying this
rather long story.

664
00:35:19,067 --> 00:35:21,700
他们先这么说，然后她又…（咕哝）
They go like this
and then she's going...
(MUTTERING)

665
00:35:21,733 --> 00:35:22,967
根本没给时间。
It's going down to
no time at all.

666
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:25,867
接着就这样，他说：“是啊。”
Then it's like this,
and he said, "Yeah."

667
00:35:25,900 --> 00:35:28,300
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

668
00:35:28,333 --> 00:35:29,533
现在，30年前你曾在Squeeze乐队，
Now, 30 years ago,
you were with Squeeze,

669
00:35:29,567 --> 00:35:31,300
那可是朋克时代的代表。
which was part
of the punk era.

670
00:35:31,333 --> 00:35:32,933
你还怀念那种胡闹吗？
Do you miss
the sort of gobbing?

671
00:35:32,967 --> 00:35:36,233
要是回到1978，他们早就对我们喷口水了。
If this was 1978,
they would just be
spitting on us.

672
00:35:36,267 --> 00:35:38,200
那简直就是一场‘goz’的冰雹。
It would just be
a hailstorm of goz.

673
00:35:38,233 --> 00:35:40,400
-老实说，那时候这算是赞美。-是啊。
-But honestly, it was a
compliment at the time.
-It was.

674
00:35:40,433 --> 00:35:42,700
-然后……-随便‘goz’我们吧。
-And then...
-Feel free to goz on us.

675
00:35:42,733 --> 00:35:45,433
那可是当年的事儿。
That was back then,
back in the day.

676
00:35:45,467 --> 00:35:47,467
不过我们的经纪人迈尔斯·科普兰说，
But then our manager,
Miles Copeland said,

677
00:35:47,500 --> 00:35:49,667
“好吧，你准备怎么讨好那些干这种事的人？”
"Well, what you going to do
to ingratiate yourself with
anybody who's doing that?"

678
00:35:49,667 --> 00:35:52,467
他说：“看，舞台侧边有几罐啤酒。”
He said, "Look, there's some
tins of beer at the side
of the stage.

679
00:35:52,500 --> 00:35:53,700
“把啤酒递过去。”
"Hand the tins of beer out."

680
00:35:53,733 --> 00:35:55,367
于是我们照做，等他们喝上啤酒后
So we did that
and once they had the beer

681
00:35:55,400 --> 00:35:57,667
-然后他们把空罐子
扔向我们。
-(观众笑)
-then they chucked
the empty cans at us.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

682
00:35:57,700 --> 00:35:59,667
你甚至还遇到过乔伊·拉莫恩。
You even met Joey Ramone.

683
00:35:59,700 --> 00:36:01,867
这里有人知道
乔伊·拉莫恩是谁吗？
Does anyone here know
who Joey Ramone is?

684
00:36:01,900 --> 00:36:05,667
是的。就一个人
已经够了，
因为这是BBC。
Yes. One person
and that's enough
because this is the BBC.

685
00:36:05,667 --> 00:36:08,667
我们不是为了收视率，
是为了那边的那个人。
We're not going for ratings,
we're going for the one man
over there.

686
00:36:08,700 --> 00:36:10,100
那感觉怎么样？
What was it like?

687
00:36:10,133 --> 00:36:12,433
我们在一个叫CBGB的俱乐部玩
We were playing in this club
called CBGB's

688
00:36:12,467 --> 00:36:14,567
那简直是个
超赞的朋克俱乐部。
which was a sort of
fantastic punk club.

689
00:36:14,667 --> 00:36:16,367
我们结束后，
他们说……
After we finished,
they said...

690
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:18,767
拉莫恩说，“想不想
下来这家俱乐部？”
Ramone said, "Do you want to
come down to this club?"

691
00:36:18,800 --> 00:36:20,733
一个叫KZ's的很不错的地方。
A very nice place called KZ's.

692
00:36:20,767 --> 00:36:25,033
于是我们去了，我真的
从未去过类似的地方，之前也没有，之后也没有。
So we went there and I really
have never been anywhere
like it before or since.

693
00:36:25,067 --> 00:36:27,800
每一个房间，
都有一场狂欢或……
Each and every room,
there was an orgy or...

694
00:36:27,833 --> 00:36:30,067
吸毒，或者各种荒诞场面。
Drug-taking or some
sort of absurd scenes.

695
00:36:30,100 --> 00:36:33,667
感觉像部奇怪的《卡里古拉》之类的电影。
It was like a strange film
of Caligula or something.

696
00:36:33,700 --> 00:36:35,167
从未见过这样的事。
Never seen anything like it.

697
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:38,000
总之，我站在那里
和其中一个拉莫恩聊天。
Anyway, I was standing there
talking to one of the Ramones.

698
00:36:38,033 --> 00:36:40,133
我低头一看，
非常惊讶
I looked down
and I was very surprised

699
00:36:40,167 --> 00:36:41,967
发现那里有
to see that there was

700
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:48,000
一个纽约的女人
在纽约进行
对他的身体做出某种动作。
one of the womenfolk
of New York performing
an act upon his person.

701
00:36:48,033 --> 00:36:50,267
你知道吗，他竟然失去
对我说的内容的兴趣！
Do you know, he rather lost
interest in what I was saying!

702
00:36:50,300 --> 00:36:52,067
(观众笑)
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

703
00:36:52,100 --> 00:36:54,567
不幸的是，
我们现在得停下。
不，别停
Unfortunately,
we must now stop.
No, we mustn't

704
00:36:54,667 --> 00:36:57,700
因为我要跟你说，
你刚出了一张新
专辑，对吧？
because I tell you something,
you've got this new
album out, yeah?

705
00:36:57,733 --> 00:37:00,800
好吧，这是很多
我们合作中的最佳作品
的合集。
Well, it's a lot of the
best of the collaborations
that we've done.

706
00:37:00,833 --> 00:37:02,700
我参与了
大量的合作，
这是最棒的一个。
I've done
lots of collaborations,
it's the best one.

707
00:37:02,733 --> 00:37:04,300
-我们找到了它的片段。
-哦，我的天哪。
-We've got a clip of it.
-Oh, my word.

708
00:37:04,333 --> 00:37:06,233
只是想说明他到底有多少
人跟他一起演出。
Just to show how many people
this guy actually plays with.

709
00:37:06,267 --> 00:37:08,000
-对电视抱歉，
但我们开始吧。
-不，没事儿。
-Sorry about the telly,
but here we go.
-No, that's all right.

710
00:37:08,033 --> 00:37:09,067
放磁带吧。
Play the tape.

711
00:37:09,100 --> 00:37:10,667
# 告诉我
